    "lawCode": "Amd §3, Chap 448 of 2017",
    "lawSection": "Canal",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6779\n\nSPONSOR: MANNION\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 448 of the laws of 2017, amending the canal law\nrelating to the upstate flood mitigation task force, in relation to\nextending the effectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis bill would amend chapter 448 of the laws of 2017 and would extend\nthe provisions of the law relating to the establishment of the upstate\nflood mitigation task force.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Amends the canal law to add a new article 13-B creating the\nupstate flood mitigation task force to identify reasonable measures that\ncan be taken to enhance flood management and mitigation, including the\ndevelopment of the upstate flood mitigation grant program.\n\nSection 2. Provides the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nOver the last decade, upstate New York has experienced some of the worst\nflooding in the state's history. In 2017 the Governor signed A6716,\nwhich established the Upstate Flood Mitigation Task Force which was to\nprovide an in-depth yet rapid assessment of flood control study sectors\nand issues related to floodplain management, debris management, flood\ncontrol, and flood mitigation in the upstate region. However, this task\nforce was not formed. Chapter 448 of 2017 was effective until March 31,\n2020. Being that flooding is still a major problem, providing an exten-\nsion to establish this task force is essential to the upkeep and\nsurvival of wildlife and infrastructure in upstate New York.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2017: A6716 - Chapter 448 of 2017\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis law shall take effect March 31, 2021 and expire July 1, 2023.\n",
